Z||000000||fierodave||10-14-2000||01:27 AM||||<BR>I want to take a minute to thank a forum member for all his help in the last few days!  <P>It makes a person thankful there are people out there that care enough to help out another person. <P>Thanks to all of you that sent email about getting well with my illness.<P>be assured I will still be selling and have a supply of parts!  <P>I just need to adjust to the condition,  and meds and i'll be ok!<P>OK......The big thanks goes out to a guy on this forum <P>Indy_resto_guy<BR>Keith came to my house in Wi from Indy to pick up some parts he purchased and ended up staying two days helping me out!!! <P>He put a water pump in my daily driver 84 coupe, and did a complete tune-up on my new 86 GT <BR>along with sorting and storeing some stuff I needed moved around!<P>Never asked for a dime either!!<P>He spent two days here because  he knew I couldn't get the pump in the car  because of my vision & such, <BR>He got out his scan tools and did a once over on my 86 GT.<P>Keith it runs better than ever!!<P>and he just dug in and did it for me!(I was going to take it to the dealer)  <P>This  guy is a top notch guy!!<BR>If any of you on this forum have a chance to deal with Keith in the future, do so knowing he is as straight as an arrow.  <P>Not many people out side of this group would do that for a person you only met a few times!<P>Just wanted to let you all know<BR>I do appreciate the support I have gotten from this Forum!!<P>It proves this is the best Forum out there.<P>Thank you  Indy_resto_guy<BR>(keith pyle) Of Indy!<BR>ready for another 18 pepper corn  blackened steak dinner?<P>Thanks for the space<BR>FD<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://members.theglobe.com/fierodave/gifs/fierosig.gif">   <P><BR><p>[This message has been edited by fierodave (edited 10-14-2000).]||||reg||14
